messages.body:
@t3dotgg self-merged PRs #27832, #29922, and #29987, adding a 30-second-idle toast after 5 sent prompts that fires `PUT user/starred/pingdotgg/t3code` with the host server's GitHub credentials.

- Bypassed Macroscope bot's `Needs Human Approval` block.
- Grew `pingdotgg/t3code` from 30k to 77k stars in 25 days (+3,094 stars/day on GitHub Trending) while watchers stayed near ~129.

When @DDdxx666 agreed to consider renaming the MIT fork to avoid confusion, @theo replied at 19:36 CST:

> "Not consider. Do it right now or I'm going to contact GitHub and have your account taken down."

@DDdxx666 renamed the repo to `Stardust` and stripped all T3 branding within 30 minutes. @theo apologized privately in DMs while leaving both 200k-view public posts up.
